1
00:01:54,570 --> 00:01:55,370
Chanchao!

2
00:01:55,570 --> 00:01:56,330
- Chanchao
- Chanchao

3
00:01:56,850 --> 00:01:57,500
Ouch!

4
00:02:00,170 --> 00:02:00,930
Thep, look.

5
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:03,290
Chanchao!

6
00:02:13,850 --> 00:02:14,650
Mr. Thep

7
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:17,490
Bu-nga is here too.

8
00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:21,250
Look at how she's dressed.

9
00:02:22,210 --> 00:02:23,530
The poor don't know their place.

10
00:02:23,970 --> 00:02:24,810
I can't stand her.

11
00:02:25,650 --> 00:02:26,810
Is there a problem?

12
00:02:26,930 --> 00:02:28,530
The room my senior booked.

13
00:02:29,010 --> 00:02:29,970
Someone's already in it.

14
00:02:30,090 --> 00:02:31,370
It's that lady.

15
00:02:31,450 --> 00:02:33,330
She just checked in half an hour ago.

16
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,280
This is Luang Dechadireksorn,

17
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:37,520
my great-grandfather.

18
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,240
I'm sorry to bother you on your first day.

19
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,480
It's fine.

20
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,040
Staying busy is good.

21
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,760
No time to overthink.

22
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:58,000
I'm sorry...

23
00:03:58,080 --> 00:03:58,880
for startling you.

24
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:00,480
Anyway,

25
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:01,760
What are you doing out here?

26
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:03,880
Well,

27
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:06,160
I'm looking for Thep.

28
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:09,280
He's been gone a while,
so I'm here to check.

29
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:11,840
But I can't find him anywhere.

30
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:14,280
He might be back in his room.

31
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:16,400
If he's still not there,

32
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:17,400
I’ll help you search.

33
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:19,520
Okay.

34
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,320
Mr. Jomthap

35
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:26,000
Yes?

36
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:28,840
I’m going to the campus,
then I’ll come back to pack.

37
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:30,960
- Got it.
- Oh and,

38
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,160
Without your help last night...

39
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,120
we’d have been in trouble.

40
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:37,760
Thanks again.

41
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,080
Don't mention it.

42
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:42,560
It's nice having company.

43
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:44,360
By the way,

44
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:45,680
found a new place?

45
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:46,720
Yes, I did.

46
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,880
It's a professor's house.

47
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:51,160
He runs an Airbnb.

48
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,280
My senior who's a teacher...

49
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:54,320
recommended it.

50
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:56,560
Actually,

51
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,600
I think...

52
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,040
this house could also be an Airbnb.

53
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:03,160
Or a small hotel.

54
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,160
I'm sure

55
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:06,560
if you opened one,

56
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:07,960
it'd always be fully booked.

57
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,960
It would cost a fortune that way.

58
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:15,080
I'd rather just sell it.

59
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,920
Someone's coming to see it today.

60
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:19,880
They'll make it...

61
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:21,800
a boutique hotel.

62
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,240
You're really selling it?

63
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:26,760
Yes.

64
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,080
I don't want to live here.

65
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,200
I'm not used to Thailand anymore.

66
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:34,280
I moved abroad at seven,

67
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:35,560
and only...

68
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,120
returned...

69
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,640
once...

70
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:39,800
after high school.

71
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,240
Now I'm here...

72
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:42,600
to sort out the inheritance.

73
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:45,160
What was the price again?

74
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,880
Only 30 million baht, Ploy.

75
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:53,520
Fully furnished, too.

76
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:55,520
Even this huge bed.

77
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:59,120
We don't have that kind of money, Thep.

78
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:07,160
Selling part of
the Charoen Nakhon building...

79
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:08,280
should be enough.

80
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,560
I really love it here.

81
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:12,040
Staying...

82
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,720
just feels incredibly right.

83
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:17,400
But I think

84
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:18,640
it's...

85
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,080
a bit creepy here.

86
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:23,000
I've done a quick check.

87
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:25,440
The structure is very solid.

88
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:27,760
It won't need much renovation.

89
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,400
How about this?

90
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:34,640
Let's have an inspector check it first.

91
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,400
If I knew you were interested,

92
00:07:41,464 --> 00:07:42,600
I would've waited.

93
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:44,840
But someone already contacted me.

94
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,880
They'll be here to see it at 4 PM.

95
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:50,680
- If they like it..
- I'll put down a 500,000 baht deposit.

96
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,480
What did you just say?

97
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:59,680
I just really love this place.

98
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:00,760
Well,

99
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:01,640
I mean...

100
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:04,240
I've never liked
a place this much before.

101
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:05,840
Ploy,

102
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:06,960
Look.

103
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:08,160
Uh,

104
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:11,000
we're not moving out.

105
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,360
I sorted it out

106
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:15,040
so we can stay here.

107
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,520
Once the transfer is done,

108
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,360
Mr. Jomthap will move out,

109
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,920
and we can do whatever we want.

110
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:27,360
Ploy

111
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:30,720
Are you mad?

112
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:32,320
Hmm?

113
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,680
No.

114
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,600
I'm just worried.

115
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,760
We just got here yesterday.

116
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:41,920
It's too soon to tell if we'll like it.

117
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,000
Ploy,

118
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:46,760
I know...

119
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:49,080
you and our kid will love it here.

120
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:57,160
Trust me.

121
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:10,280
Just come and take a look.

122
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:27,200
Peekaboo!

123
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:36,240
Peekaboo!

124
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,920
See? I told you.

125
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:47,200
I'm going to work now.

126
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:49,080
Okay.

127
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,320
Peekaboo!

128
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:08,760
Peekaboo!

129
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,120
Mommy!

130
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,880
Mommy

131
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:14,960
- Ma'am
- Are you hurt?

132
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,440
I'm fine.

133
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:18,680
I just got scared.

134
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:24,200
Chanchao

135
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:26,640
Who were you playing with?

136
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:31,040
Hmm.

137
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:34,720
She's been by herself the whole time.

138
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:45,800
Let's go.

139
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,160
You're hurt again.

140
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:50,520
I think

141
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,400
you should visit the temple.

142
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:54,120
You'll feel better,

143
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,600
and have some good luck.

144
00:12:58,280 --> 00:12:59,440
Any suggestions?

145
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,220
Do you want to tag along?

146
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:05,160
I'm heading that way.

147
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:55,740
Just call me, and I'll pick you up.

148
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:57,400
That's alright.

149
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:59,200
I can go back with Thep.

150
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:00,120
Thank you.

151
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:01,400
Okay.

152
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:02,960
Let's go.

153
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:09,240
After you.

154
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:51,680
Get the fortune sticks for me, honey.

155
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:53,720
Yes.

156
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:00,400
Thank you.

157
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:33,840
Number 14 brings ill fortune.

158
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:37,360
Past karma summons impending doom.

159
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:41,480
Like a pierced warrior, tread with care.

160
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:45,280
Pause and reflect upon your path.

161
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:49,680
Foes from former lives shall return,

162
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:53,680
Bringing despair and the urge to flee.

163
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:58,120
Persevere in your righteous deeds.

164
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:02,920
To shield your life from certain death.

165
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:14,000
What...

166
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:16,720
do they mean?

167
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:19,520
Oh.

168
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:22,280
Well,

169
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,360
if it's a bad fortune, just burn it.

170
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:27,840
Sorry?

171
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:31,180
If it's bad,

172
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:32,720
don't take it with you.

173
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:34,360
Go burn it over there.

174
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:36,960
The fortune teller isn't here.

175
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:40,240
He could see your fortune
and perform a cleansing ritual.

176
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,780
But he should be back soon.

177
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:45,320
Do you want to wait?

178
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:47,280
He's very accurate.

179
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:49,120
No, thank you.

180
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,000
Maybe next time.

181
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:52,800
I'll be around for a while anyway.

182
00:16:53,160 --> 00:16:53,980
Thank you.

183
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:55,200
Come back soon.

184
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:57,140
Come back soon.

185
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,160
Yum-yum.

186
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:15,240
Do you want to feed yourself?

187
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:16,240
Totally.

188
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:26,640
Is the food alright?

189
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,160
Is it too spicy?

190
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,720
I think she likes it.

191
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,840
See, she can't stop eating.

192
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,280
It's amazing.

193
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,840
It's not spicy at all.

194
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:45,840
She wasn't raised on spicy food,
but she handles it better than us.

195
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:48,360
Then she's perfect for the South.

196
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:53,480
This place feels like home.

197
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:56,520
If you had room, I’d definitely stay.

198
00:17:57,800 --> 00:17:59,080
There's always next time.

199
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:02,200
And...

200
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:04,000
where are you staying now?

201
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:07,040
Luang Decha's place.

202
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:09,440
Wait...

203
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,560
No one has lived there for years.

204
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:15,380
I used to sneak in and play there
when I was little.

205
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:18,600
Did you...

206
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,600
ever see anything weird there?

207
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:22,960
No, never.

208
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:26,840
But actually,
it was pretty creepy.

209
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:37,640
Glad you're enjoying the food.

210
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:39,920
Let me get you some snacks.

211
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,360
On the house.

212
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:43,120
Thank you.

213
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:44,800
I'll be right back.

214
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:51,640
When is Dad coming?

215
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:55,840
Soon. He said he's done with his errands.

216
00:19:00,600 --> 00:19:01,840
More water?

217
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,480
All done now?

218
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:12,240
Just left the dean's office.

219
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:14,920
About the house,
I'm staying put.

220
00:19:15,040 --> 00:19:16,040
I'll explain later.

221
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:17,360
And...

222
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:19,960
Do you know any consulting firms?

223
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:21,760
I want to renovate the house.

224
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:25,680
Yes.

225
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:31,920
Here.

226
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:33,280
Your payment.

227
00:19:34,720 --> 00:19:35,480
Thank you.

228
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:40,360
Actually,

229
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:41,560
I still have one more.

230
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,400
- Another piece?
- Yes.

231
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:44,160
Let me see.

232
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:47,640
Here.

233
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:53,600
What a shame.

234
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:55,320
The dial is cracked.

235
00:20:00,840 --> 00:20:01,800
How about...

236
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:03,680
I'll give you 120,000 baht?

237
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:06,480
150,000 baht, please.

238
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:10,600
No worries if you can't.

239
00:20:11,680 --> 00:20:13,120
Hold on a second.

240
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:17,320
Khem.

241
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:18,680
Don't!

242
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:21,840
Fine.

243
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:24,040
150,000 baht it is.

244
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:26,680
It's antique gold after all.

245
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:28,840
Wait for me right here.

246
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,240
You're just in time.

247
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:34,240
You...

248
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:35,320
go...

249
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:37,360
get the money for his watch.

250
00:20:37,680 --> 00:20:38,560
150,000 baht.

251
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:41,600
We have no cash right now.

252
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:46,280
I'm sorry.

253
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:47,800
Actually,

254
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,840
we're in a rush to run errands.

255
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:51,520
Errands?

256
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:52,920
What errands?

257
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,200
Important ones.
I'll tell you later.

258
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:57,800
Excuse us.

259
00:20:57,880 --> 00:20:58,720
We're not buying it.

260
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:01,040
- We're closing the shop.
- Okay.

261
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:06,440
Hey,

262
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:07,640
You!

263
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:09,520
What's wrong?

264
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:27,520
Khem.

265
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:32,900
Are you mad at me?

266
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:53,240
You said you wouldn't be mad.

267
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:55,000
No matter what I did.

268
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:58,520
Who said I was mad?

269
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:00,480
Exactly.

270
00:22:01,040 --> 00:22:02,100
That's what I thought.

271
00:22:02,480 --> 00:22:04,840
I don't even know
what I did to make you mad.

272
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:07,760
If I ever make you mad,

273
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:08,680
just tell me.

274
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:09,720
Okay.

275
00:22:37,480 --> 00:22:38,580
Thank you.

276
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:03,120
Bu-nga...

277
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:07,360
Do you know...

278
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:09,740
why I gave you the watch?

279
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:14,780
Because it represents time.

280
00:23:17,920 --> 00:23:19,440
Time is the most valuable thing.

281
00:23:20,120 --> 00:23:21,440
It never returns.

282
00:23:27,360 --> 00:23:28,560
Giving time...

283
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:32,080
is giving a part of your life.

284
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:35,820
It's a shame...

285
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:38,540
that the watch has stopped.

286
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:53,180
It means...

287
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:55,940
my time...

288
00:23:57,760 --> 00:23:59,160
has stopped with you.

289
00:25:16,040 --> 00:25:17,540
I wasn't mad at all.

290
00:25:20,680 --> 00:25:22,580
Not at all.

291
00:25:24,760 --> 00:25:26,180
Never once.

292
00:25:28,960 --> 00:25:30,300
But I was hurt.

293
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:12,760
Sir!

294
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:21,200
Are you alright?

295
00:26:21,920 --> 00:26:22,720
I'm fine.

296
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:23,800
Thank you so much.

297
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:31,400
Are you sure you don’t want a doctor?

298
00:26:32,120 --> 00:26:33,680
I'm not hurt at all.

299
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:37,480
My eyes have been blurry for a while.

300
00:26:37,960 --> 00:26:38,960
It's getting worse.

301
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:40,640
Forget it.

302
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:42,720
I'll be dead in a few years anyway.

303
00:26:44,320 --> 00:26:45,360
Why would you say that?

304
00:26:45,880 --> 00:26:48,240
I've seen some live to be a hundred.

305
00:26:49,360 --> 00:26:51,320
Why live that long?

306
00:26:52,080 --> 00:26:54,400
Those who passed have all been reborn.

307
00:27:00,520 --> 00:27:02,000
I should get going.

308
00:27:02,520 --> 00:27:03,640
I have things to do.

309
00:27:06,240 --> 00:27:07,760
You're selling something.

310
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:09,440
Don't bother.

311
00:27:11,800 --> 00:27:13,540
Some things already have owners.

312
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:15,640
We shouldn’t touch them.

313
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:21,440
Who is the owner?

314
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:25,200
You'll find out someday.

315
00:27:29,400 --> 00:27:31,040
You're not from around here?

316
00:27:32,560 --> 00:27:33,160
No,

317
00:27:33,440 --> 00:27:34,220
I'm not.

318
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:36,400
Where are you staying now?

319
00:28:02,360 --> 00:28:03,720
Are you from that family?

320
00:28:04,080 --> 00:28:04,660
I am.

321
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:08,360
People in that family don't live long.

322
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:10,320
None of them make it to 50.

323
00:28:11,960 --> 00:28:13,220
It's a curse.

324
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:14,920
Who cursed them?

325
00:28:15,440 --> 00:28:18,000
The owner of what you're selling.

326
00:28:18,760 --> 00:28:20,520
Why did they curse us?

327
00:28:23,760 --> 00:28:25,160
They hated your ancestors.

328
00:28:27,520 --> 00:28:28,120
So...

329
00:28:28,320 --> 00:28:29,960
Aren’t they part of my family?

330
00:28:30,840 --> 00:28:32,640
Then why is it in my house?

331
00:28:35,160 --> 00:28:36,440
Find that out for yourself.

332
00:28:57,560 --> 00:28:58,160
Here you go.

333
00:29:02,880 --> 00:29:04,040
It's amazing.

334
00:29:04,280 --> 00:29:05,200
Thank you so much.

335
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:06,640
Try some.

336
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:08,120
Sure.

337
00:29:13,120 --> 00:29:13,760
Thep.

338
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:16,860
Dad is here.

339
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:22,360
I knew you’d be here from downstairs.

340
00:29:23,680 --> 00:29:25,504
It's a lovely place, isn't it?

341
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:28,560
This is Mr. Danai, the owner.

342
00:29:29,080 --> 00:29:29,800
Hello.

343
00:29:30,320 --> 00:29:31,360
Nice to meet you.

344
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:33,760
I saw the lobby.

345
00:29:33,960 --> 00:29:35,320
The hotel is so lovely.

346
00:29:35,736 --> 00:29:37,080
Thank you very much.

347
00:29:37,760 --> 00:29:39,320
This town is so cozy.

348
00:29:39,720 --> 00:29:40,600
I feel...

349
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:42,920
just like at home.

350
00:29:44,400 --> 00:29:45,240
Who knows?

351
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:47,560
Maybe you lived in Songkhla in a past life.

352
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:51,900
Maybe so.

353
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:55,040
I heard you just arrived.

354
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:56,560
You haven't seen much yet, right?

355
00:29:56,880 --> 00:29:58,920
Once Ploy's leg is fully healed,

356
00:29:59,120 --> 00:30:00,480
we'll explore more.

357
00:30:00,816 --> 00:30:03,120
For now, we're just driving around town.

358
00:30:08,040 --> 00:30:10,520
Hey, what's wrong?
Since when do you drink?

359
00:30:13,480 --> 00:30:14,440
What's up with you, Khem?

360
00:30:14,872 --> 00:30:16,200
Drinking in broad daylight.

361
00:30:21,008 --> 00:30:22,640
They say getting drunk helps you forget.

362
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:24,320
Forget?

363
00:30:25,800 --> 00:30:27,040
What do you want to forget?

364
00:30:33,440 --> 00:30:34,480
Did someone hurt you?

365
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:37,620
No one.

366
00:30:39,280 --> 00:30:40,380
Don't lie to me.

367
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:42,720
We grew up together.
How could I not know?

368
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:43,760
Khem,

369
00:30:44,280 --> 00:30:45,760
I love you like my own brother.

370
00:30:46,440 --> 00:30:47,480
If anyone hurts you,

371
00:30:47,680 --> 00:30:49,120
I’ll make sure they pay for it.

372
00:30:58,280 --> 00:30:58,960
Khem.

373
00:30:59,720 --> 00:31:00,700
Hold on, Khem.

374
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:02,460
Hey, what the...

375
00:31:06,320 --> 00:31:06,920
Hey!

376
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:09,720
Don't you two know Dam?

377
00:31:11,360 --> 00:31:13,000
I do apologize for him.

378
00:31:13,120 --> 00:31:13,720
Brothers.

379
00:31:14,880 --> 00:31:16,160
That sounds...

380
00:31:16,320 --> 00:31:17,280
much better.

381
00:31:18,040 --> 00:31:20,340
Just give us 300 baht for the damages.

382
00:31:22,240 --> 00:31:22,920
300 baht?

383
00:31:23,440 --> 00:31:25,300
And I'll let him go.

384
00:31:25,960 --> 00:31:28,160
I don't have that much on me.

385
00:31:28,760 --> 00:31:30,000
- That's bullshit.
- Hey!

386
00:31:33,240 --> 00:31:34,560
So, do we have a deal?

387
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:39,400
If you take any longer,

388
00:31:39,720 --> 00:31:41,000
or if I get jumpy,

389
00:31:41,240 --> 00:31:42,560
the price goes up.

390
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:48,120
- Hey!
- Hey!

391
00:32:02,600 --> 00:32:05,280
Hey, go fight somewhere else!

392
00:32:06,320 --> 00:32:08,160
- Hey!
- Go fight somewhere else!

393
00:32:09,120 --> 00:32:10,840
Wait, he's Luang Decha's son.

394
00:32:10,880 --> 00:32:12,560
- Decha's son!
- Quick! Move!

395
00:32:26,720 --> 00:32:27,740
Thep.

396
00:32:28,840 --> 00:32:29,400
Thep.

397
00:32:29,880 --> 00:32:30,680
Thep!

398
00:32:32,480 --> 00:32:35,280
Are you alright?
I've been calling you.

399
00:32:36,440 --> 00:32:37,240
I'm sorry.

400
00:32:37,600 --> 00:32:39,280
I was just lost in thought.

401
00:32:40,880 --> 00:32:42,200
Shall we head back?

402
00:32:42,840 --> 00:32:43,520
Sure.

403
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,120
Excuse us.

404
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:49,760
Please come again.

405
00:32:50,280 --> 00:32:50,760
Sure.

406
00:32:50,880 --> 00:32:51,480
Thank you.

407
00:32:51,640 --> 00:32:52,240
You're welcome.

408
00:33:13,320 --> 00:33:15,240
People in that family don't live long.

409
00:33:15,600 --> 00:33:17,240
None of them make it to 50.

410
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:21,240
It's a curse.

411
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:22,920
Who cursed them?

412
00:33:24,240 --> 00:33:26,880
The owner of what you're selling.

413
00:34:02,880 --> 00:34:03,760
Thep

414
00:34:11,080 --> 00:34:12,320
I'm fine.

415
00:34:13,136 --> 00:34:14,660
Nothing serious.

416
00:34:15,800 --> 00:34:16,680
Look at Khem.

417
00:34:17,720 --> 00:34:18,800
He's much worse than me.

418
00:34:20,200 --> 00:34:22,440
If he wasn't drunk,
this wouldn't have happened.

419
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:26,360
Did you eat yet?

420
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:27,480
I'll....

421
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:29,920
My son doesn't eat just anything.

422
00:34:36,760 --> 00:34:38,280
I spoke with the doctor.

423
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:40,360
You can go home today.

424
00:34:41,200 --> 00:34:42,620
But my doctor...

425
00:34:43,080 --> 00:34:44,440
said I need two days of rest.

426
00:34:44,960 --> 00:34:47,280
Our family doctor is sending someone
for a home check-up.

427
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:51,448
It's not safe here.
Too many snakes around.

428
00:34:54,400 --> 00:34:56,920
I don't think so.

429
00:34:57,280 --> 00:34:58,440
I only see toads.

430
00:34:58,760 --> 00:34:59,760
What toads?

431
00:34:59,960 --> 00:35:01,200
You're talking nonsense, Phon.

432
00:35:02,080 --> 00:35:03,960
A toad on a palanquin.

433
00:35:04,920 --> 00:35:06,340
You're going too far.

434
00:35:06,920 --> 00:35:08,920
No need to say more, son.

435
00:35:11,480 --> 00:35:12,160
Phon

436
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:13,080
Khem

437
00:35:14,480 --> 00:35:16,080
Help Thep pack for home.

438
00:35:16,352 --> 00:35:17,280
Got it.

439
00:35:22,240 --> 00:35:24,280
We'll wait in the doctor's office.

440
00:35:30,320 --> 00:35:31,120
As for you,

441
00:35:31,920 --> 00:35:33,020
you can go now.

442
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:54,720
- My goodness!
- Phon!

443
00:35:55,240 --> 00:35:58,160
My bad.
I didn't mean that.

444
00:35:58,440 --> 00:36:00,000
I was picking up your glasses.

445
00:36:00,120 --> 00:36:00,480
I'll...

446
00:36:00,600 --> 00:36:02,760
make you a new one at home.

447
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:04,480
Oh dear.

448
00:36:10,680 --> 00:36:12,220
I'm so sorry.

449
00:36:27,400 --> 00:36:29,160
Keep it even, Phon.

450
00:36:30,200 --> 00:36:32,000
You startled me.

451
00:36:32,160 --> 00:36:33,400
You've lost your touch.

452
00:36:34,120 --> 00:36:35,800
I'm getting old.

453
00:36:35,920 --> 00:36:37,800
My eyesight is failing.

454
00:36:37,960 --> 00:36:40,040
I’ve done this since I was 18.

455
00:36:41,480 --> 00:36:42,160
Phon

456
00:36:42,520 --> 00:36:43,160
Yes?

457
00:36:45,800 --> 00:36:46,520
My dear

458
00:36:49,600 --> 00:36:50,440
I have good news.

459
00:36:52,160 --> 00:36:53,440
What is it?

460
00:36:59,400 --> 00:37:00,960
My friend wrote to me...

461
00:37:01,120 --> 00:37:03,420
there's a vacancy
at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

462
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:04,860
Phon

463
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:05,512
Yes?

464
00:37:05,560 --> 00:37:07,500
- Go get Thep.
- Yes.

465
00:37:10,760 --> 00:37:12,280
That's a relief.

466
00:37:14,280 --> 00:37:16,400
I wish we’d known sooner.

467
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:17,920
That's on you.

468
00:37:18,440 --> 00:37:20,200
You're always so slow.

469
00:37:21,240 --> 00:37:22,960
I thought you wanted him home.

470
00:37:23,360 --> 00:37:24,680
So I didn’t hurry.

471
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:26,520
That's true.

472
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:29,280
He is the apple of my eye.

473
00:37:29,720 --> 00:37:30,840
But it's better...

474
00:37:31,360 --> 00:37:33,280
to send him far away...

475
00:37:33,560 --> 00:37:35,200
than have him wed a peasant.

476
00:37:36,032 --> 00:37:38,240
My husband also took one.

477
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:40,800
It’s beyond embarrassing.

478
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:41,840
Hey,

479
00:37:42,560 --> 00:37:44,060
come on.

480
00:37:44,960 --> 00:37:47,220
Where did that come from?

481
00:37:51,400 --> 00:37:54,000
You’re the only one I love.

482
00:37:55,320 --> 00:37:56,120
I’m serious.

483
00:38:12,632 --> 00:38:14,720
You must marry Bu-nga...

484
00:38:14,880 --> 00:38:16,620
before you leave for the capital.

485
00:38:16,960 --> 00:38:19,020
Mother will never ask for her hand.

486
00:38:21,440 --> 00:38:22,980
Then you’ll have to elope.

487
00:38:40,160 --> 00:38:41,580
It's been days.

488
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:44,080
Why aren't you better yet?

489
00:38:51,840 --> 00:38:53,600
I'll take you to the doctor tomorrow.

490
00:38:54,840 --> 00:38:56,440
Don't worry, Father.

491
00:38:56,600 --> 00:38:58,420
Mother is already taking me.

492
00:39:12,320 --> 00:39:13,320
Last month...

493
00:39:13,440 --> 00:39:15,040
she ran out to be sick...

494
00:39:15,160 --> 00:39:16,440
right in the middle of a dance.

495
00:39:16,640 --> 00:39:17,160
Wait.

496
00:39:17,240 --> 00:39:19,020
Isn't she unmarried?

497
00:39:19,120 --> 00:39:21,560
Then how is she with child?

498
00:39:22,200 --> 00:39:23,592
Who else could the husband be?

499
00:39:23,760 --> 00:39:24,880
It's Khem...

500
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:26,520
Luang Decha's servant.

501
00:39:26,600 --> 00:39:27,680
But you know,

502
00:39:27,880 --> 00:39:29,960
Khem's been chasing her for a while.

503
00:39:30,120 --> 00:39:31,520
Funny she’s only just fallen pregnant.

504
00:39:32,160 --> 00:39:32,600
Yeah.

505
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:33,440
I know...

506
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:34,880
who the real father is.

507
00:39:35,400 --> 00:39:36,480
It's not Khem.

508
00:39:39,040 --> 00:39:40,400
- Watch your mouth.
- Khem! Khem!

509
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:43,160
- Khem! Khem!
- Khem!

510
00:39:43,600 --> 00:39:44,160
Khem!

511
00:39:44,560 --> 00:39:45,200
Khem!

512
00:39:45,640 --> 00:39:47,240
Stop it, Khem!

513
00:39:47,440 --> 00:39:48,160
Stop!

514
00:39:51,240 --> 00:39:51,880
Khem!

515
00:39:52,040 --> 00:39:53,120
He was badmouthing you.

516
00:40:00,760 --> 00:40:02,800
If Bu-nga were a man,

517
00:40:03,560 --> 00:40:04,360
she'd be...

518
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:07,660
even more famous than you.

519
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:10,560
Nora...

520
00:40:11,200 --> 00:40:12,640
is in our blood.

521
00:40:13,280 --> 00:40:14,600
It's who we are.

522
00:40:15,480 --> 00:40:16,640
Whether you're a man

523
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:18,840
or a woman.

524
00:40:19,120 --> 00:40:20,040
Women...

525
00:40:20,360 --> 00:40:21,840
simply can't be ordained...

526
00:40:22,840 --> 00:40:24,720
or perform certain rituals.

527
00:40:24,960 --> 00:40:26,360
But they can all...

528
00:40:26,720 --> 00:40:28,080
become the leading Nora.

529
00:40:29,000 --> 00:40:30,400
And I believe...

530
00:40:30,640 --> 00:40:31,440
one day,

531
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:33,200
my girl...

532
00:40:33,480 --> 00:40:35,320
will outshine any man.

533
00:40:35,360 --> 00:40:38,000
Well, well!

534
00:40:38,160 --> 00:40:42,480
I bet she'll get knocked up first.

535
00:40:45,720 --> 00:40:46,240
Look...

536
00:40:46,320 --> 00:40:46,920
over there.

537
00:40:47,800 --> 00:40:52,080
Khem's guarding her like a watchdog.

538
00:40:52,280 --> 00:40:53,480
Hey, Phon.

539
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:54,368
What?

540
00:40:54,840 --> 00:40:55,680
What do you want?

541
00:40:57,560 --> 00:40:58,740
Did you come here...

542
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:00,760
just to bark at us?

543
00:41:01,160 --> 00:41:03,040
Are you calling me a dog, Nui?

544
00:41:03,800 --> 00:41:04,120
You...

545
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:05,900
Phon!

546
00:41:06,160 --> 00:41:07,440
Just spit it out.

547
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:23,400
Gently!

548
00:41:23,720 --> 00:41:24,120
That hurts.

549
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:27,720
You weren't hurting...

550
00:41:27,840 --> 00:41:28,520
while you were fighting.

551
00:41:29,200 --> 00:41:29,600
Right?

552
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:35,160
I hate it when you pick fights like this.

553
00:41:36,360 --> 00:41:37,520
I had to!

554
00:41:38,040 --> 00:41:39,120
He insulted you.

555
00:41:39,520 --> 00:41:41,440
And he was about to drag Thep into it.

556
00:41:45,400 --> 00:41:46,120
Gently! Gently!

557
00:41:46,192 --> 00:41:46,760
It hurts!

558
00:41:56,760 --> 00:41:57,820
Ouch!

559
00:42:01,280 --> 00:42:01,680
Bu-nga!

560
00:42:01,760 --> 00:42:02,240
Bu-nga!

561
00:42:03,080 --> 00:42:03,480
That hurts!

562
00:42:06,640 --> 00:42:08,020
Ouch!

563
00:42:34,720 --> 00:42:36,640
People in that family don't live long.

564
00:42:37,000 --> 00:42:38,640
None of them make it to 50.

565
00:42:58,160 --> 00:42:59,060
Hello, Mom.

566
00:43:01,800 --> 00:43:03,180
How old was Dad when he died?

567
00:43:05,960 --> 00:43:06,800
48.

568
00:43:08,680 --> 00:43:09,280
Oh, no...

569
00:43:09,560 --> 00:43:10,480
It's nothing.

570
00:43:12,520 --> 00:43:13,280
Thanks.

571
00:43:43,160 --> 00:43:45,280
Father, please stop!

572
00:43:45,760 --> 00:43:47,280
Please!

573
00:43:48,680 --> 00:43:49,640
Being a Nora,

574
00:43:49,880 --> 00:43:51,200
you must behave.

575
00:43:53,160 --> 00:43:54,520
Even if you can't be ordained

576
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:56,080
or become a Nora master,

577
00:43:57,000 --> 00:43:58,600
you must remain virtuous.

578
00:43:58,800 --> 00:43:59,640
Keep your morals.

579
00:44:00,040 --> 00:44:00,760
Uphold your dignity.

580
00:44:01,640 --> 00:44:02,880
Behaving like this,

581
00:44:03,320 --> 00:44:05,840
how will you face our ancestors?

582
00:44:06,040 --> 00:44:06,960
Master!

583
00:44:09,040 --> 00:44:10,240
Please stop hitting her.

584
00:44:10,640 --> 00:44:12,040
She's pregnant.

585
00:44:12,200 --> 00:44:13,840
Are you the father or something?

586
00:44:13,960 --> 00:44:14,600
Khem!

587
00:44:15,080 --> 00:44:15,840
Not him.

588
00:44:16,200 --> 00:44:16,840
I am.

589
00:44:18,560 --> 00:44:19,400
Mr. Thep

590
00:44:28,600 --> 00:44:29,800
Bu-nga is my wife.

591
00:45:05,160 --> 00:45:06,280
Only Father...

592
00:45:08,920 --> 00:45:09,960
and Khem...

593
00:45:12,360 --> 00:45:14,200
truly love me.

594
00:45:22,840 --> 00:45:24,920
I'm so sorry.

595
00:45:28,040 --> 00:45:30,520
Mr. Thep and I really love each other.

596
00:45:31,080 --> 00:45:32,880
We were just too impatient.

597
00:45:33,840 --> 00:45:34,840
If you’re ashamed,

598
00:45:36,240 --> 00:45:38,040
you can tell them all.

599
00:45:39,480 --> 00:45:41,160
I’ll just run away.

600
00:45:41,320 --> 00:45:43,400
Tell them I’m no good...

601
00:45:43,720 --> 00:45:45,920
that you’ve disowned me.

602
00:45:46,760 --> 00:45:48,360
I'm not worried about myself.

603
00:45:49,280 --> 00:45:51,560
I just hate seeing you suffer.

604
00:45:54,360 --> 00:45:55,120
Father

605
00:45:56,440 --> 00:45:57,800
Please, listen.

606
00:45:58,200 --> 00:45:59,480
Don't you worry.

607
00:45:59,800 --> 00:46:03,120
He promised to
take good care of the kid and me.

608
00:46:04,360 --> 00:46:07,200
He's sending his parents to propose.

609
00:46:07,960 --> 00:46:08,560
I...

610
00:46:08,680 --> 00:46:10,160
know how the world works.

611
00:46:10,720 --> 00:46:12,640
It won't be that easy.

612
00:47:01,040 --> 00:47:02,040
They must rot in pain...

613
00:47:03,560 --> 00:47:04,520
and drown in misery.

614
00:47:05,880 --> 00:47:06,920
Left with nothing.

615
00:47:08,920 --> 00:47:10,880
Just as they did to us.

616
00:47:17,760 --> 00:47:19,080
It's all set.

617
00:47:19,280 --> 00:47:22,600
I'll be home to pack and
head to the airport.

618
00:47:23,040 --> 00:47:24,280
Thank you so much...

619
00:47:24,400 --> 00:47:25,320
for sorting this out.

620
00:47:53,360 --> 00:47:54,000
Ploy,

621
00:47:55,720 --> 00:47:56,920
we'll talk later.

622
00:47:57,240 --> 00:47:58,240
I have a class to get to.

623
00:47:59,760 --> 00:48:00,340
Okay.

624
00:48:14,280 --> 00:48:14,760
Alright.

625
00:48:14,920 --> 00:48:16,680
Now, let's look at...

626
00:48:21,560 --> 00:48:22,240
Picture B.

627
00:48:24,200 --> 00:48:25,440
What Photoshop tool...

628
00:48:25,560 --> 00:48:26,560
was used for this?

629
00:48:28,440 --> 00:48:29,540
Clone Stamp.

630
00:48:30,560 --> 00:48:31,280
Correct.

631
00:48:57,520 --> 00:48:58,160
Hey!

632
00:48:58,600 --> 00:48:59,520
Why don't you...

633
00:49:23,280 --> 00:49:24,240
Professor?

634
00:49:26,080 --> 00:49:27,120
Professor?

635
00:49:29,160 --> 00:49:30,240
Professor!

636
00:49:31,120 --> 00:49:31,640
Yes?

637
00:49:32,080 --> 00:49:34,200
- Time's up.
- Time's up?

638
00:49:44,080 --> 00:49:44,880
- Oh.
- Hey!

639
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:45,560
Where are you off to?

640
00:49:45,960 --> 00:49:47,520
I'm picking Ploy up from the airport.

641
00:49:47,680 --> 00:49:49,000
So I won't be heading back here.

642
00:49:49,200 --> 00:49:49,640
I see.

643
00:49:50,400 --> 00:49:51,480
It's been months.

644
00:49:52,120 --> 00:49:53,960
Hope you don't get lost
like your first day.

645
00:49:54,680 --> 00:49:55,400
I won't.

646
00:50:17,280 --> 00:50:18,420
Which part do you need me to explain?

647
00:50:18,880 --> 00:50:20,400
From the start.

648
00:50:32,000 --> 00:50:33,960
Everyone knows by now...

649
00:50:34,280 --> 00:50:35,800
that you're with that woman.

650
00:50:35,920 --> 00:50:37,480
I'm here to beg you.

651
00:50:38,000 --> 00:50:39,920
Please, ask for Bu-nga’s hand for me.

652
00:50:40,080 --> 00:50:42,760
She will never be my daughter-in-law.

653
00:50:43,560 --> 00:50:44,360
Hello?

654
00:50:45,240 --> 00:50:45,920
Ploy?

655
00:50:49,360 --> 00:50:50,440
Is the signal bad?

656
00:50:51,000 --> 00:50:51,600
Yeah.

657
00:50:51,760 --> 00:50:53,680
I hear music in the background.

658
00:50:53,960 --> 00:50:55,100
It’s a Nora song.

659
00:50:56,680 --> 00:50:57,760
What did you say?

660
00:50:58,280 --> 00:51:00,580
Have you told your parents...

661
00:51:01,120 --> 00:51:02,280
about the baby and me?

662
00:51:05,600 --> 00:51:07,120
If Bu-nga is really pregnant...

663
00:51:07,280 --> 00:51:09,160
it’s likely Khem’s baby.

664
00:51:10,160 --> 00:51:12,160
They’re always together.

665
00:51:12,360 --> 00:51:13,560
Are you looking for someone?

666
00:51:13,840 --> 00:51:15,360
I'm here for the fortune teller.

667
00:51:15,560 --> 00:51:16,520
Wait here.

668
00:51:18,280 --> 00:51:19,520
I had a weird dream.

669
00:51:20,600 --> 00:51:21,920
I've never had a dream like that before.

670
00:51:23,000 --> 00:51:24,320
It was about a woman.

671
00:51:25,560 --> 00:51:26,760
Could she be the owner?

672
00:51:27,000 --> 00:51:30,400
Persevere in your righteous deeds.

673
00:51:30,720 --> 00:51:34,720
To shield your life from certain death.

674
00:51:35,920 --> 00:51:37,840
I hope it's not too late.

675
00:52:11,640 --> 00:52:12,440
Chanchao!
